# Task 2: Authentication & Role Routing Implementation Plan

As Principal Full-Stack Developer, this plan outlines the architecture for **Supabase Authentication**, **Role-Based Routing**, and **Edge Middleware Route Protection** for our custom LMS.

---

## Architecture & Authentication Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Student / Teacher
    participant Browser as Browser (Next.js Client)
    participant Action as Server Action (actions/auth.ts)
    participant SupabaseAuth as Supabase Auth (auth.users)
    participant DB as Supabase PostgreSQL (public.profiles)
    participant Middleware as Edge Middleware (middleware.ts)

    Note over User,Browser: Sign Up Flow
    User->>Browser: Enters email, password, full_name, selects Role (student/teacher)
    Browser->>Action: Form submit -> signup(formData)
    Action->>SupabaseAuth: supabase.auth.signUp({ email, password, options: { data: { full_name, role } } })
    SupabaseAuth-->>DB: DB Trigger: handle_new_user() creates public.profiles row
    SupabaseAuth-->>Action: Auth Session & User created
    Action-->>Browser: Redirect to /student/dashboard or /teacher/dashboard

    Note over User,Browser: Login & Role Redirection
    User->>Browser: Submits email & password on /login
    Browser->>Action: Form submit -> login(formData)
    Action->>SupabaseAuth: supabase.auth.signInWithPassword({ email, password })
    Action->>DB: Query public.profiles WHERE id = user.id (read role)
    alt Role == 'teacher'
        Action-->>Browser: Redirect to /teacher/dashboard
    else Role == 'student'
        Action-->>Browser: Redirect to /student/dashboard
    else Role == 'admin'
        Action-->>Browser: Redirect to /admin/dashboard
    end

    Note over Browser,Middleware: Subsequent Protected Route Requests
    Browser->>Middleware: Request /teacher/dashboard
    Middleware->>SupabaseAuth: Verify JWT & fetch session user
    alt User is student trying to access /teacher/*
        Middleware-->>Browser: Redirect 307 -> /student/dashboard?error=unauthorized
    else Valid Teacher
        Middleware-->>Browser: Allow (NextResponse.next())
    end
```

