## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Dashboard Routes Alignment**:
> The user specified:
> - Teacher redirection: `/teacher/dashboard`
> - Student redirection: `/student/dashboard`
> 
> In Task 1, routes were at `/teacher` and `/student`. We will create:
> - `src/app/(dashboard)/teacher/dashboard/page.tsx`
> - `src/app/(dashboard)/student/dashboard/page.tsx`
> - `src/app/(dashboard)/admin/dashboard/page.tsx`
> And configure `/teacher` and `/student` to seamlessly rewrite or redirect to their `/dashboard` sub-paths for complete backwards compatibility.
>
> **Role Resolution in Middleware**:
> When a user logs in, Supabase stores `role` inside `user.user_metadata.role` (which is encoded in the JWT session cookie). The middleware checks `user.user_metadata.role` instantly without incurring an extra network roundtrip database query on every edge request! If metadata is missing, it falls back to querying `public.profiles`.

